[13:50:43.465036] commit a3e4dba46fff45d65743b02ef65afb3185d0c15b
[13:50:43.465042] Author: Byungkwan Kim <byungkwan.kim@cnu.ac.kr>
[13:50:43.465046] Date:   Mon Sep 7 00:58:02 2026 +0000
[13:50:43.465050] 
[13:50:43.465055]     feat(pec): lattice ownership contract — one realized-edge source for volumes, sheets, wires; two_plane deleted (#931, stage A)
[13:50:43.465059]     
[13:50:43.465064]     rfx/boundaries/pec.py now carries the #931 contract: an E component is PEC
[13:50:43.465068]     iff its own location is inside the closed conductor region.
[13:50:43.465073]     
[13:50:43.465077]     - realized_pec_edge_masks(cell_mask, sheets, wires, periodic): the only
[13:50:43.465081]       function turning geometry into PEC edges. Volume rule = four incident
[13:50:43.465086]       cells (backward shifts under the #689 convention, one spelling `_shift`);
[13:50:43.465090]       sheet rule = union footprints per normal axis, both end nodes with the
[13:50:43.465094]       forward in-plane shift; wire = edges of the axis-aligned lattice path.
[13:50:43.465098]     - SheetSpec (frozen; full-shape one-layer footprint, static plane),
[13:50:43.465102]       WireSpec + wire_path_edge_masks (diagonal segment raises).
[13:50:43.465106]     - realized_wall_planes(edge_masks, axis, *, ij=None, region=None),
[13:50:43.465110]       edge_is_pec, clear_edges, apply_pec_edges; apply_pec_mask is a wrapper
[13:50:43.465114]       (periodic, sheets) — no two_plane_mask kwarg.
[13:50:43.465118]     - apply_pec_occupancy: noisy-OR of the four incident cells with the same
[13:50:43.465122]       shifts applied to the OCCUPANCY (a zero pad reads "no conductor"),
[13:50:43.465127]       periodic flags, static sheet_edge_masks OR'd in; bit-identical to the hard
[13:50:43.465131]       rule at binary occupancy on the battery (faces 0 and n-1, seam, 2-D lane).
[13:50:43.465135]     - Deleted: two_plane_extension_masks, _place_at_next_plane.
[13:50:43.465139]       tangential_edge_masks kept only as the pre-#931 classification the f0
[13:50:43.465143]       sheet ctx and sheet_normal_live_axis_masks still read (TODO stage B).
[13:50:43.465159]     - simulation.py / nonuniform.py per-step calls drop two_plane_mask;
[13:50:43.465163]       simulation.py hands the run's periodic flags to the soft path too.
[13:50:43.465168]     - tests/contracts/test_lattice_ownership_contract.py: §5 battery (slab
