[13:50:43.566682] a3e4dba46fff45d65743b02ef65afb3185d0c15b
[13:50:43.566691] 2026-09-07 00:58:02 +0000
[13:50:43.566696] Byungkwan Kim
[13:50:43.566710] feat(pec): lattice ownership contract — one realized-edge source for volumes, sheets, wires; two_plane deleted (#931, stage A)
[13:50:43.566714] 
[13:50:43.566721] rfx/boundaries/pec.py now carries the #931 contract: an E component is PEC
[13:50:43.566726] iff its own location is inside the closed conductor region.
[13:50:43.566730] 
[13:50:43.566734] - realized_pec_edge_masks(cell_mask, sheets, wires, periodic): the only
[13:50:43.566738]   function turning geometry into PEC edges. Volume rule = four incident
[13:50:43.566742]   cells (backward shifts under the #689 convention, one spelling `_shift`);
[13:50:43.566746]   sheet rule = union footprints per normal axis, both end nodes with the
[13:50:43.566761]   forward in-plane shift; wire = edges of the axis-aligned lattice path.
[13:50:43.566767] - SheetSpec (frozen; full-shape one-layer footprint, static plane),
[13:50:43.566770]   WireSpec + wire_path_edge_masks (diagonal segment raises).
[13:50:43.566775] - realized_wall_planes(edge_masks, axis, *, ij=None, region=None),
[13:50:43.566779]   edge_is_pec, clear_edges, apply_pec_edges; apply_pec_mask is a wrapper
[13:50:43.566783]   (periodic, sheets) — no two_plane_mask kwarg.
[13:50:43.566787] - apply_pec_occupancy: noisy-OR of the four incident cells with the same
[13:50:43.566791]   shifts applied to the OCCUPANCY (a zero pad reads "no conductor"),
[13:50:43.566795]   periodic flags, static sheet_edge_masks OR'd in; bit-identical to the hard
[13:50:43.566799]   rule at binary occupancy on the battery (faces 0 and n-1, seam, 2-D lane).
[13:50:43.566803] - Deleted: two_plane_extension_masks, _place_at_next_plane.
[13:50:43.566807]   tangential_edge_masks kept only as the pre-#931 classification the f0
[13:50:43.566811]   sheet ctx and sheet_normal_live_axis_masks still read (TODO stage B).
[13:50:43.566815] - simulation.py / nonuniform.py per-step calls drop two_plane_mask;
[13:50:43.566819]   simulation.py hands the run's periodic flags to the soft path too.
[13:50:43.566823] - tests/contracts/test_lattice_ownership_contract.py: §5 battery (slab
[13:50:43.566827]   t=1..3 per axis, sheet, footprint, mirror/permutation, soft==hard, wire,
[13:50:43.566831]   helpers, API-level sheet/G4/sub-cell/grep). On the old rule all 9 slab
[13:50:43.566835]   cases failed "FAR FACE MISSING"; now 77/81 pass — the 4 reds need the
[13:50:43.566839]   rasterizer stage (pec_sheets collector, sub-cell refusal, two_plane
[13:50:43.566844]   removal from api/visualize/etc.).
[13:50:43.566847] - tests/locks/test_two_plane_pec_slab.py deleted (design note §2).
[13:50:43.566851] 
[13:50:43.566857] R3: memory=rfx-known-issues.md("top face plane is never zeroed" 2026-08-28; two_plane A/B verdict) | R2-attempts=0 (redesign, not a repeat) | falsifier=§5 slab battery t=1,2,3 on each axis + soft≡hard at binary incl. faces 0/n-1 and the periodic seam (tests/contracts/test_lattice_ownership_contract.py)
